-- title:
--   Attachment of the supersingular annulus at the zero chart
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose residue field $k$ has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed, and let $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar p` be the subfield of the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by base change from $\mathbb Q$-subfield generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q^d)$, $d \mid p$. Let $Fbar0$ be a field extension of $k$ and $C_0$ a component chart for $F$ along $A$ with values in $Fbar0$: a valuation subring $C_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$, a surjective reduction map onto $Fbar0$ with kernel the maximal ideal, a set $C_0.\mathrm{dom}$ of places of $F/\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a finite set $C_0.\mathrm{nodes}$ of places of $Fbar0/k$, a map on places, and the compatibility axioms of `ComponentChart`. Assume given $X \in Fbar0$ and places $xpl(c)$ of $Fbar0/k$, $c \in k$, such that for every polynomial $P$ over $k$ the order of $P(X)$ at $xpl(c)$ is the multiplicity of $c$ as a root of $P$; that the elements $j$ and $j_p := j(q^p)$ of $F$ lie in $C_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with reductions $X^p$ and $X$ respectively; and that $a \in k$ satisfies $a^{p^2}=a$, $a \neq 0$, $a \neq 1728$, and lies in `ssJSet p k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no non-zero point killed by $p$. Assume $xpl(a^p) \in C_0.\mathrm{nodes}$. Let $An$ be an annulus for $F$ along $A$ (domain, parameter, modulus in the maximal ideal of $A$, together with the rationality, evaluation, unique-centre, simple-zero and unit axioms of `Annulus`) whose parameter is $j_p - j^p$ and whose domain consists exactly of those places $W$ for which there are $x,y \in A$ with residues $a$ and $a^p$ such that $W$ has strictly positive order at $j - x$ and at $j_p - y$. Assume further two compatibility hypotheses between $C_0$ and reduction of modular functions: first, any $g \in F$ whose Fricke transform `frickeInvolutionBar p g` lies in the localised modular ring `CharPReduction.modularLocalized p A.toSubring` and has non-zero image under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom` lies in $C_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with non-zero reduction; second, for $g \in C_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose Fricke transform lies in that localised ring and reduces into `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the order at $xpl(a^p)$ of the reduction of $g$ equals the order of that reduced function at the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k (a ^ p)`. Then $An$ is attached to $C_0$ at $xpl(a^p)$: the place $xpl(a^p)$ is a node of $C_0$, the parameter $j_p-j^p$ lies in $C_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its reduction has order $1$ at $xpl(a^p)$, and for every $f \in C_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with non-zero reduction and order $0$ at every place of $An.\mathrm{dom}$, and every such place $P$, the element $P(f)\,P(An.\mathrm{param})^{-\operatorname{ord}_{xpl(a^p)}(\bar f)}$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there.
--
--   This is the attachment of the supersingular annulus of $X_0(p)$ at $p$, with parameter $j(q^p)-j(q)^p$, to the chart of the component carrying the cusp $0$, at the node lying over the supersingular $j$-invariant $a$; it records the three clauses of attachment (node, simple zero of the parameter, slope law) for the semistable-chart formalism. It feeds the level-one specialisation [`ModularCurve.isAttached_ssAnnulus_zeroChart_of_chartSpec_levelOne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isAttached_ssAnnulus_zeroChart_of_chartSpec_levelOne).
